<title>FRANCE: France wants &quot;solid currency&quot; - Jospin.</title>
<headline>France wants &quot;solid currency&quot; - Jospin.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>French Prime Minister Lionel Jospin said on Friday France wanted a solid currency.</p>
<p>He said in a radio interview that the rise in the dollar was good in some ways. But it made imports, for example of oil, more expensive, he said. &quot;Every coin has its reverse side,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>&quot;We want to have a solid currency,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom, +33 1 42 21 53 81</p>
</text>
